Tier: T4
Why: Device pushes put text on locked screens and act on push tokens; a fault leaks health, message or booking detail to anyone holding the phone, or targets the wrong device.
T4 trigger scan: lock-screen copy (privacy of health and message content), push tokens (device identity), migration 20270307000000 (new PushOutbox table, RLS, backfill), account-deletion manifest entry.
T3 trigger scan: notification preferences and quiet hours (user consent and timing).
Bounded T1: NO (migration, privacy boundary, tokens, more than one module).
Canonical builder: T4 builder lane B-PUSH2-120 (agent 120 wave).
Parent owner: operator (agent 120 wave).
Acceptance evidence: test/push-lock-screen-copy.spec.ts; Sol P1 probe 6/6 and Opus live L5/L6 on Postgres at 346cf4a8 (ci-lane run 37350591060); every required PR check green at the exact head; Opus and Sol verdicts at the exact head.
Promotion triggers: already T4. Any change to lock-screen templates, token handling, the migration or the deletion manifest needs fresh dual exact-head verdicts.

